    {
      "id": "vesta-appliances-from-impostors-to-proof-of-trust-ATYNCN",
      "sector": "manufacturing",
      "title": "Vesta Appliances: from impostors to Proof-of-Trust",
      "summary": "Vesta Appliances is a fictional Swiss manufacturer with a very real problem: forty years of brand trust and no way to prove it online. Customers chat with fake support agents trading on Vesta's name, impostor technicians ring doorbells in Vesta livery, and nothing distinguishes the real services from the fakes.\n\nThe use case shows how Vesta becomes verifiable on the Verana Network, a public decentralized registry of registries. Its support chatbot and staff portal present ECS Service and Organization credentials as Linked Verifiable Presentations in their DID Documents, employees carry verifiable badges, repair partners hold Authorized Repairer accreditations issued under Vesta's own ecosystem governance. Anyone can resolve a Vesta service and see Proof-of-Trust before connecting: TRUSTED is earned from the credential chain, never just claimed.\n\nIt all runs live on the Verana testnet playground as an interactive story with runnable demos: verify the support chat from a personal wallet, check a technician's accreditation at the front door, and sign into the portal with a badge credential. Services are hosted by VS Agent, Verana's open-source business wallet.",
